# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trellis. Copy to `.env` for local development, and set the same keys in the
# Vercel project for production.
#
# In Vercel: tick ALL THREE environments (Production / Preview / Development)
# on every variable, and do NOT mark anything "Sensitive" — sensitive variables
# become write-only, so a failed save is indistinguishable from a successful
# one. Environment changes need a redeploy to take effect. /settings renders
# the resolved values the running function actually sees; trust it over the
# dashboard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Database (Supabase Postgres) -------------------------------------------
# The connection POOLER string, transaction mode, port 6543 — not the direct
# connection. Serverless functions are short-lived and numerous and a direct
# connection's limit cannot absorb that. The direct hostname is also IPv6-only
# on newer Supabase projects and is not reachable everywhere; a connection that
# hangs with no error is usually this.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/trellis

# --- Deployment --------------------------------------------------------------
# The STABLE production domain. The same value goes in the GitHub Actions
# repository variable APP_URL — never a per-deployment URL, which changes on
# every deploy and makes the scheduler silently no-op.
APP_URL=

# --- Instagram Graph API ------------------------------------------------------
# Pinned deliberately and shown on /settings. Verified live on the previous
# build: requests sent to v21.0 came back with v26.0 in every response URL.
GRAPH_API_VERSION=v21.0
IG_HANDLE=
IG_USER_ID=
IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# The token needs SEVEN scopes. See lib/graph/scopes.ts.
#   instagram_basic, instagram_manage_insights, instagram_manage_comments,
#   pages_read_engagement, pages_show_list, business_management,
#   instagram_content_publish
# business_management is the one that fails silently: without it,
# GET /me/accounts returns {"data": []} — empty, not an error.

# --- Model provider ------------------------------------------------------------
# No model name appears anywhere outside lib/model/provider.ts. Format is
# `provider:model`. MODEL_FALLBACK is the second lane — free model catalogues
# change without notice and providers have deleted models running code depended
# on.
MODEL_PRIMARY=google:gemini-3.6-flash
MODEL_FALLBACK=
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# --- Cron auth -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sent as `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` by Vercel's cron caller and by
# the GitHub Actions schedules. Store the identical value as the repository
# secret CRON_SECRET. Required in production — the guard returns 503 rather
# than running unauthenticated if it is missing there.
CRON_SECRET=
